---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description={`About ${siteConfig.name}: a family-oriented HTML5 game portal with curation, guides, and clear policies.`}
  showSearch={false}
>
  <article class="container-arcade prose-arcade legal-doc w-full max-w-4xl py-8 sm:py-10">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-white">About {siteConfig.name}</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-arcade-muted leading-relaxed">
      {siteConfig.name} is a lightweight, fully static browser game portal operated by {siteConfig.legalName}.
      We help people discover free HTML5 games through search, categories, continue-playing tools on your device,
      and short how-to notes—so you can play in the browser without installing an app-store client.
    </p>

    <h2>Our mission</h2>
    <p>
      Deliver a fast, accessible, family-oriented discovery experience that works on phones, tablets, and desktops.
      The Site is generated as plain HTML and hosted on CDNs such as Cloudflare Pages or GitHub Pages.
    </p>

    <h2>How we add value</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Organized categories and search across a curated catalog</li>
      <li>Per-game pages with controls guidance, similar titles, and click-to-play loading</li>
      <li>Original help content (FAQ, policies, accessibility information) beyond raw feed dumps</li>
      <li>Client-only continue/favorites tools stored in your browser</li>
      <li>Content screens intended to reduce adult, port/piracy-style, and other high-risk inventory</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where games come from</h2>
    <p>
      Titles are aggregated from public HTML5 distribution feeds (such as GameMonetize and GameArter), then
      normalized into a local catalog and filtered against our Content Policy. Each game remains the intellectual
      property of its original publisher or developer. Embedded games may include their own advertising or branding
      inside the sandboxed play frame.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      We may display third-party advertisements (for example Google AdSense) in clearly labeled slots outside the
      game viewport. See our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> and{' '}
      <a href="/content-policy/">Content Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to meet WCAG 2.2 Level AA where practical for a static entertainment site. Read our{' '}
      <a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility Statement</a> for details and how to report barriers.
    </p>

    <h2>Copyright</h2>
    <p>
      See our <a href="/dmca/">DMCA / Copyright Policy</a> for intellectual property notices.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
